      "top_findings": [
        "t_gate: run_cell_gate (test_l3tc_tail_gate.py:1062) is the per-cell L3-TC gate. For opt=='supergrok2' it SHORT-CIRCUITS to _sg2_l3tc_gate.run_sg2_gate (:1075-1077) BEFORE any factory call — that is why _CELLS registers supergrok2/{decoder,vit,mamba} with factory=None (:536-538); it's by design, not dead.",
        "t_gate: THE fp64+A/A/A gate lives at test_l3tc_tail_gate.py:1338-1418 — (1a) params rel_err<param_tol; (1b) STATE m/v/ema<1e-4 is THE DECISIVE check (step-1 update collapses to sign so 1a is blind to beta1/state-init); (2) A/A/A via _one() x3 with torch.equal on loss/grad/params. RE-ANCHOR task #10: references are now fp64 ref_<opt>_step (test_reference_parity.py), eager per-op kernels DELETED.",
        "t_gate: run_sg11_warmup_gate (test_l3tc_tail_gate.py:882) sets rescale=2.0, runs warmup_steps, recovers the kernel's per-tensor gate via least-squares sg_k=(k_m-beta1*m0)/(1-beta1) (:988), verdict gate_ok=(err_vs_momentum<1e-2 and err_vs_mu>1e-1) (:1013) — FIXED kernel uses cos(grad,momentum) not the buggy cos(grad,mu).",
        "t_gate: _build_cell (test_l3tc_tail_gate.py:551) reseeds torch.manual_seed+cuda.manual_seed_all immediately BEFORE build_model (:567) because build_model draws from the global RNG (not c['seed']) — load-bearing for the A/A/A determinism gate.",
        "t_oracles: test_reference_parity.py defines the fp64 ref_<opt>_step per optimizer (single source csrc/algorithms/<opt>.h): ref_adamw (:68), ref_lion (:76), ref_grokadamw (:88), ref_grokfast (:101), ref_neuralgrok (:109), ref_looksam_apply (:131), ref_prodigy_apply (:172, step size is d NOT lr), ref_sg11 (:189), ref_sg15 (:227), ref_sg2_apply (:240, lamb_eff RESTORED), ref_muon (:270). REFERENCE_OPTIMIZERS registry of 11 (:297).",
        "t_oracles: mamba_oracle.py is the Mamba-1 oracle (28 tensors, total 259425, oracle_loss_and_grads :612); mamba3_oracle.py is the Mamba-3 SISO oracle (manual complex-trapezoidal scan bwd vs autograd <=1e-10, model_forward/backward :663/:685). These are TWO distinct oracles for two distinct kernels.",
        "t_tc: layouts pinned — decoder 30 tensors total 422755 (decoder_oracle.py:187), vit 32 tensors 418017 (vit_oracle.py:204), mamba-1 28 tensors 259425, mamba-3 toy 45 tensors 593713 (test_mamba_tc.py:98). The kernel mirrors assert recompute==forward (decoder_kernel_mirror.py:201, vit_kernel_mirror.py:235) — a load-bearing structural check.",
        "t_tc: the KEYSTONE TC gate is _bf16_faithful_oracle (test_decoder_tc.py:390 / test_vit_tc.py:290 / test_mamba_tc.py:165) — model fwd+bwd in fp64 with bf16 ONLY at the kernel's exact storage points, so a real bug shows rel~1 while bf16 noise stays at the calibrated floor (weights 0.15, biases 0.08). decoder loss tol tightened to 1e-4 to CATCH a real bias-omission bug (test_decoder_tc.py:527-534).",
        "t_tc: dW GEMM isolation (test_decoder_tc.py:633 / test_vit_tc.py:567 / test_mamba_tc.py:530) dumps the kernel's OWN bf16 operands, fp32-contracts ascending-t, asserts rel<1e-4 — the ff2.weight Kin=512 4-N-tile path the engine micro-gates never exercised. ViT adds gridstride (cap=1) + ragged (B=80) keystones (test_vit_tc.py:521/531).",
        "t_rest: _sg2_l3tc_gate.run_sg2_gate (:128) validates the SG2 TC megakernel vs the PURE-fp64 oracle_step from sg2_kernel_mirror (B1, max|Δ{param,m,v,mu,slow,gru}|<1e-5) using _strategy_a_perm (:77, lexsort |g|+idx = the in-kernel bitonic sort total order) + A/A/A + tie-probe + the N>64 CSA fidelity REPORT (won't-grok gap, NOT a regression).",
        "t_rest: the parallelism gates carry the fixed-order/ascending-reduce A/A/A discipline with BIT-EXACT asserts: sharded_optimizer (test_sharded_optimizer.py:234, torch.equal vs P3 tail), dp2/pp2 loopback, tp_loopback (5 asserts incl. transport-neutrality vs serial chunked-order), zero3 roundtrip (save/resume bit-exact + drifted-plan/rank RAISE), step_graph_capture (HONEST: no-collective spine captured, megakernel+collective NOT). pp2 PATCH-GATED on .phase2/patches/0001 (SG_DECTC_LAYER_RANGE).",
        "t_nonhw: conftest.py registers the single 'hw' marker. test_shard_map/test_pipeline_schedule/test_zero3_plan are pure-CPU host mirrors of the shard/pipeline/zero3 plans (cross-checked by the GPU gates). tests/tpu/test_pallas_parity_interpret.py validates all 11 Pallas TPU launch_<opt>_step (interpret=True) vs the fp64 refs at fp32 tol 1e-4/1e-3 — tpu_v6e PRESERVED, skips cleanly without jax."
