        "BUILD_AND_VALIDATE.md:15-43 — TWO L3 model-stage designs co-exist: the early element-local SURROGATE (model_stages.cuh: acts[gi]=GELU(params[gi]+input[gi]), NOT real model math, race input int tokens != float[numel]) and the REAL per-model stages (model_stage_{decoder,vit,mamba3}.cuh + fused_*_megakernel.cuh). The surrogate L3 cells are now DEAD on the race path (real decoder/vit/mamba routed first in fused_step). Lever (a) L1 = real PyTorch fwd+bwd + fused optimizer.step (opt_only=True).",
        "DESIGN-TC-PIPELINE.md:32 — CONTRADICTION with PROJECT TRUTH (R2 PLANNING doc, predates the L3-TC build): §0 claims 'NO in-kernel wgmma; every model-stage GEMM is scalar fp32 owner-computes triple loop; only WGMMA path is host-launched CUTLASS in mma.cuh'. This is the PRE-TC state the doc PLANNED to fix; production is now in-kernel wgmma L3-TC. Its smem numbers (decoder 42KB/vit 188080B/mamba 145124B) are the SCALAR SampleSmem, contradicted by .campaign_plan #14's measured d-INDEPENDENT TC megakernel smem 13.7/7.7/14.8KB.",
        ".campaign_plan.md:147-167 — #14 SMEM CLIFF REFUTED: TC megakernel smem d-INDEPENDENT (acts stage through HBM workspace not smem). The 'vit/mamba smem cliff' was the DEAD SCALAR fallback kernel (wiring 33/33 never uses it; ptxas-hard-stops decoder TU at d>=768). 0.49% FINDING: d=1024 decoder still 0.49% roofline (compute-regime) — inefficiency lives in WGMMA ENGINE/kernel structure, ~60-100x headroom. C7515 wgmma serialization STILL PRESENT after H1 (WARPGROUP.DEPBAR after every HGMMA); true overlap needs cp.async mbarrier ring (blocked on bf16 weight pre-stage + TMA-transpose + 255regs/2.6KB spills).",
        "PHASE1_CAMPAIGN.md:42-73 + MAMBA3_REFERENCE.md:1-22 — Mamba-3 upgrade (Mamba-1 SelectiveSSMLayer -> genuine Mamba-3 arXiv 2603.15569): Phase 1 reference + fp64 oracle DONE+validated (manual backward matches autograd <=4e-15; canonical 1.528B), but Phases 2-4 (L3-TC megakernel, re-gate 11 cells, HIP/Pallas) NOT done — 'CUDA megakernel untouched, nothing committed'. INTEGRATION-MAMBA.md still describes the OLD Mamba-1 (28 tensors/259425 elems). Mamba CANNOT fit d=2048 roofline (MambaSampleSmem dynamic crosses 227KB at ~d=142; stays at production d=128).",
        "SUPEROPTIMIZER_SCOPING.md:12-34,232-238 — NO-GO on full GPU-kernel superoptimizer. No surveyed IR (CuTe/Triton/MLIR-Linalg/polyhedral) can express the fused-training megakernel as one persistent kernel (host-launched collective can't run device-side inside persistent grid). DECISIVE: bit-exact A/A/A requires ascending-k fp32 reduction order -> legal space = TRANSPORT-ONLY rewrites. Component STOKE on dW = NO-GO (no SASS assembler on NVIDIA; lever is gmem layout above instruction window).",
        "PHASE4_REPORT.md:22-29 + BUILD_REPORT.md:188-205 — fuse-tier estimates (🟡, ptxas is arbiter): WS1 register pass promoted sm_90 L3 10->33, total L3 53->77 / L1 46->22. H100_MAXIMALITY_REPORT GAP-1: exactly ONE kernel in 456-kernel binary spills 8B = CUTLASS TF32 A-transposed RS_TN GEMM, RUNTIME-DEAD (float A-transposed path returns cudaErrorNotSupported, falls back to scalar); --maxrregcount 192/255 does NOT clear it (tested).",
        "vit_findings.md:1-96 — ViT L3-TC hill-climb 716.85->206.00ms (3.48x), frac 0.0016->0.0055: single-accumulator C7515 spill fix, dw_biases 132x-redundancy removal (ran on ALL 132 CTAs, no nCTA guard) + clspos stride-kSeq, dw_biases warp-parallel K-reduction (grad_assembly 871->7.6ms). Coalesced dW staging REVERTED (m-major coalescing -> compensating smem bank conflict). This is the empirical source of the '~97% staging' P0-revert mechanism cited in OPTIMIZATION_LEDGER."
